                            <comment id="20102662" author="gklesse" created="Thu, 2 Jul 2026 18:19:18 +0200"  >&lt;p&gt;&#129302; &lt;b&gt;Automated Complexity Analysis&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Estimate:&lt;/b&gt; L&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;b&gt;Files Affected:&lt;/b&gt; 6&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Reasoning:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
This story requires enhancing the audit trail reporting system to capture additional actions (text field and file operations: add, modify, trash). This involves both backend changes to capture and store audit events for these operations, and frontend/reporting changes to display them in a review-friendly format. The GxP compliance context and the need for targeted audit trail review indicates this touches regulatory compliance requirements, which is critical business logic.&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Implementation Details:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Backend changes needed: 1) Update audit trail event capture logic to record text field modifications (add, modify, trash operations) - likely in the experiment model or service layer where these operations occur. 2) Enhance file operation tracking to capture add, modify, and trash events with appropriate metadata. 3) Modify the audit trail report generation logic to include these new event types in the output format. Frontend/Report changes needed: 4) Update the audit trail report template/component to display text field and file operation events in a review-friendly format suitable for GxP compliance. 5) Ensure proper formatting and grouping of these events for audit review purposes. The story references updating previous work (&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.jnj.com/browse/JGVT-25&quot; title=&quot;Reports_Audit Trail: Experiment Audit Trail- Ad hoc report generation&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;JGVT-25&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;JGVT-25&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;/&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.jnj.com/browse/JGVT-2663&quot; title=&quot;Reports_Audit Trail: Experiment Audit Trail- At Signoff report generation&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;JGVT-2663&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;JGVT-2663&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;) suggesting integration with existing audit infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Open Questions:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;alternate&quot; type=&quot;square&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;What specific metadata should be captured for file operations (file name, size, type, timestamp)?&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;How should &apos;old versus new value&apos; be handled for files if not technically feasible as noted in dev notes?&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;What constitutes a &apos;review friendly format&apos; - are there specific GxP compliance formatting requirements?&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Should text field changes show full old/new values or just indicate a change occurred?&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Are there specific audit trail retention or archival requirements for these new event types?&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Should the report support filtering by event type (text vs file operations)?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Risks:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;alternate&quot; type=&quot;square&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Touches regulatory compliance (GxP) audit trail requirements - errors could have compliance implications&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Integration with existing audit trail infrastructure (&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.jnj.com/browse/JGVT-25&quot; title=&quot;Reports_Audit Trail: Experiment Audit Trail- Ad hoc report generation&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;JGVT-25&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;JGVT-25&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;/&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.jnj.com/browse/JGVT-2663&quot; title=&quot;Reports_Audit Trail: Experiment Audit Trail- At Signoff report generation&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;JGVT-2663&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;JGVT-2663&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;) may have unexpected dependencies&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;File operation tracking may have performance implications if files are large or operations frequent&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Old vs new value tracking for files noted as potentially not possible - may require design decision or workaround&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&amp;#8212;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;em&gt;This is an AI-generated complexity assessment based on the story description and codebase analysis. The development team has final authority on sizing decisions and may adjust this estimate based on their technical expertise and implementation approach. This assessment is meant to provide guidance, not to constrain technical decisions.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
