                <customfields>
                                                <customfield id="customfield_10300" key="com.atlassian.jira.plugin.system.customfieldtypes:textarea">
                        <customfieldname>Acceptance Criteria</customfieldname>
                        <customfieldvalues>
                            <customfieldvalue>&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;1) Audit&lt;/b&gt;&#160;&lt;b&gt;Trail data processing - ad hoc initiation (&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.jnj.com/browse/JGVT-25&quot; title=&quot;Reports_Audit Trail: Experiment Audit Trail- Ad hoc report generation&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;JGVT-25&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;JGVT-25&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;b&gt;Given&lt;/b&gt; a Signals Experiment with a GxP experiment template (GxP-GMP all versions)&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;b&gt;When&lt;/b&gt;&#160;the User requests an ad hoc audit trail report via an external action in the actions dropdown (&quot;GxP Experiment Audit Trail&quot;) of the experiment header, regardless of the state of the experiment&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;b&gt;Then&lt;/b&gt;&#160;th&lt;font color=&quot;#172b4d&quot;&gt;e System shall start extracting the entire experiment history data, &lt;ins&gt;&lt;b&gt;including text field and file object actions,&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/ins&gt; via an asynchronous action, and notifies the user &quot;The audit trail report is being generated.&quot;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;2) Audit Trail data processing - at initial&lt;/b&gt;&#160;&lt;b&gt;&amp;amp; subsequential&lt;/b&gt;&#160;&lt;b&gt;signing (&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.jnj.com/browse/JGVT-2663&quot; title=&quot;Reports_Audit Trail: Experiment Audit Trail- At Signoff report generation&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;JGVT-2663&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;JGVT-2663&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;b&gt;Given&lt;/b&gt; a Signals Experiment with a GxP experiment template (GxP-GMP all versions)&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;b&gt;When&lt;/b&gt; the User signs (sign and invite reviewers) the GxP experiment as author or the Reviewer signs to accept the GxP-experiment&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;b&gt;Then&lt;/b&gt; the System shall start extracting the entire experiment history data, &lt;ins&gt;&lt;b&gt;including text field and file object actions,&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/ins&gt;&#160;via an asynchronous action.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;3) Generate excel or pdf experiment audit trail report (&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.jnj.com/browse/JGVT-2698&quot; title=&quot;Reports_Audit Trail: download audit trail report via web user interface&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;JGVT-2698&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;JGVT-2698&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;b&gt;Given&lt;/b&gt; the audit trail data processing step is completed&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;b&gt;When&lt;/b&gt; the signals user accesses the the web user interface and clicks the download link for the pdf or excel audit trail report&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;b&gt;Then&lt;/b&gt;&#160;the pdf or excel audit trail report includes the entire experiment history data, &lt;ins&gt;&lt;b&gt;including text field and file object actions&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/ins&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</customfieldvalue>

                        </customfieldvalues>
                    </customfield>
